{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/582851-first-time-scion-gm-help-wanted","id":582851,"title":"first time Scion GM help wanted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-07T16:40:58-07:00","id":582851,"title":"first time Scion GM help wanted","content":"The Story:<br /> <br /> Hades is working overtime in order to finish up fixing the underworld after the Titans escaped and he is something like 80% complete, but he is still missing a Big 3 headed piece before finishing and no one has seen Cerberus in a long while... so the task of recovering him is up to the Players Band.<br /> <br /> The twist,<br /> <br /> Fate has dictated that to capture the Creature alive the Band has to prove being worthy of something only Hercules has made before, so they should also pass 11 almost Imposible Task before capturing Cerberus<br /> <br /> The Help Needed<br /> <br /> while i want the task to be easy to recognize as paralels to Hercules Labours. i dont want to make this story so Greek centric, so i want your help, comming up whit variants of this task involving the other Mythologies here is a list of the 12 Labours, and variations i have come up with<br /> <br /> <br /> Slay the Nemean Lion. (I want this to stay the same)<br /> <br /> Slay the nine-headed Lernaean Hydra. (such a clasic fight i wish it was later in the list may be at number 4)<br /> <br /> Capture the Ceryneian Hind.<br /> <br /> Capture the Erymanthian Boar. (hercules meet the Centaurs during this task, so i want my characters to meet other friendly minions, maybe Draven or Tengu)<br /> <br /> Clean the Augean stables in a single day.<br /> <br /> Slay the Stymphalian Birds.<br /> <br /> Capture the Cretan Bull.<br /> <br /> Steal the Mares of Diomedes.<br /> <br /> Obtain the girdle of Hippolyta, Queen of the Amazons. (i want to face my players whit Fanfir and get his cursed Ring)<br /> <br /> Obtain the cattle of the monster Geryon. (maybe confront a diferent breed of Giant)<br /> <br /> Steal the apples of the Hesperides.<br /> <br /> Capture and bring back Cerberus. (This will obiusly be the same)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4856-alfanumerico","name":"alfanumerico","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T21:56:45-07:00","id":583190,"title":"","content":"What level are we talking about here? Hero, low-Demigod, high-Demigod? Heracles was probably fairly high Legend to tackle the Labors. <i>Tons</i> of Epics and lots of Arete. But, here's some spitball ideas that might help. It all really depends on how close to the Labors you want to get. Heracles wasn't exactly a sneaky guy. All the labors are <i>really</i> straight forward. They're basically &quot;this monster is causing problems, go capture it&quot; <i>or</i> &quot;steal me this valuable thing&quot;. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Capture the Golden Hind -- Capture the Firebird from Slavic mythology. Just a different kind of shiny, sacred, super-speedy creature. <br /> <br /> Capture the Erymanthian Boar -- Two ideas here. One: stick with the Centaur idea, but use the biker-centaurs from Scion:Hero. They're a pretty cool way to update an ancient myth to a modern setting. So instead of capturing a giant boar, the Scions have to capture a stolen &quot;hog&quot;... in the form of a magical motorcycle created by one of the other Crafting Gods like Svarog, Wayland, Brigit, Shango, etc. Second idea: Use dwarves as your &quot;helpful/harmful&quot; minions (remember, the centaurs got drunk and attacked everyone, not exactly friendly) and sub in Garm, the hound of Hel, for the Boar.<br /> <br /> Clean the Augean Stables -- Use something like a nuclear waste dump or chemical spill, or maybe the Great Pacific Garbage Patch instead of stables. Infest it with Nemean vermin (rats, roaches, etc) or minor mythological creatures of filth and waste. Japan and Egypt have tons of those. Egypt has demons like &quot;One Who Eats The Excrement Of His Hindquarters&quot; and &quot;He Who Drinks The Blood Of The Slaughterhouse&quot;. <br /> <br /> Stymphalian Birds -- The whole challenge here was that Heracles couldn't attack the birds directly, so he had to flush them out first. Almost any monster that is hard to attack head-on could work here. Anything that possesses people or is intangible (wraiths, hungry ghosts, etc) could work really easily. If you want birds specifically, I can't think of a lot of evil mythical birds. Tengu, maybe, who are evil as often as they are good. Cherokee Raven-Mockers? It really depends on how close you want to stick to the Labors. You could go way far out and make the Scions find a non-violent solution to something like a flight of Aztec Hummingbirds (reincarnated warriors who served Huitzilopochtli) is harassing a town because the town has somehow dishonored Big H and now he's angry with them. But they can't kill the birds, because then Big H will be mad at them.<br /> <br /> Capture the Cretan Bull -- To stick with the Bull thing, there's the Sumerian Bull of Heaven that Ishtar tosses around to cause trouble. Or literally <i>any other</i> rampaging monster from <i>any</i> mythology. The challenge here is just &quot;rampaging monster&quot;. Nothing else.<br /> <br /> The Mares of Diomedes -- Foals of Sleipnir that they need to capture/steal/collect? You're really limited in horse mythology, since generally magical horses were pretty good things to have. The man-eating, fire-breathing mares involved here are kinda odd. But, again, it can be pretty much <i>any</i> magical monster depending on how far from the actual Labors you want to go.<br /> <br /> The Golden Apples -- You're in luck, because Golden Apples are common as hell. The Norse have the Golden Apples of Idunn which grant agelessness to the Norse Gods, and the Russians have Golden Apples that Ivan Tsarovitch has to get back for the same king that sends him after the Firebird. The Romanians and Bulgarians have a version where a three-headed dragon (a zmey) steals the golden apples from a king and he needs a hero to get them back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T05:19:38-07:00","id":583396,"title":"","content":"First off, Thank you that\u00b4s really helpfull<br /> <br /> now back to buisness<br /> <br /> Power level: i plan to play it at Hero-Low Demigod, where every body starts at legend 2 or 3 and then &quot;Level Up&quot; (should it be &quot;Legend Up&quot;?) every 3 or 4 labours so they are firmly in Demigod territory when finishing the labours, then if my players like the game plan a diferent quest that takethem all the way up to God and after that full on Titan war<br /> <br /> The main Reason i want to start by Slaying the Nemean Lion, is to drive home early the &quot;this are the 12 labours&quot; point, so i can start parting away from the labours to get more room of manouver whit them<br /> <br /> Capture the Firebird, i like this but a clasic Slavic faery tail may be to obscure to my players, they may just think it is a Phoenix the hole time, so to twist them once more i will probably choose a Benu (also a good point to introduce a Side/suport character i am planning to use a Scion of Anubis on a similar quest to the players)<br /> <br /> Capture Garm: Sadly we are from Mexico so the Boar/Hog joke (awsome as it is) will be lost in translation, so i will go whit te Draves/Garm idea, i realy like the Horsemen i should toss them somewhere. the thing is i plan to shift places between this task and the Hydra one. Herc Vs Hydra is probably the most clasic Hero vs Monster Story and i want it to be the &quot;Legend Up&quot; Battle, also by meeting the Draves in their second quest i give my players early access to crafting contacts so they can use any number of Trophies they get from the monsters. but using Garm i dont know, he is to close to Cerberus to be faced so early in the quest maybe another creature?<br /> <br /> Clean the Nuclear waste: i like this as a chance to face some Crazy ass Chimeras and Nemeans, maybe even the centaurs, i can see good old Ixion using nuclear waste as a fancy new ingridient for his &quot;Craft&quot;, but i will put some study in the egiptian demons as well<br /> <br /> Stymphalian Birds: this one is hard because i like both the wraiths and the Hummingbirds, as the players have not face yet anything Dead or Aztec, maybe a mix of both maybe Eagle Warriors that manifest as Hummingbirds.<br /> <br /> Rampaging Monster Challenge: i am thinking Zipacna <br /> <br /> Canibal Horse Challenge: What about the Kelpie...<br /> <br /> Golden Apple Challenge: i have this idea, of a Scion on the Edge of Falling who somehow get the one Golden Apple used to Start the trojan war (to the fairest one) and will be willing to trade it for the Andavarinaut (Cursed ring of Fafnir) said apple will be the final piece they will need to find Cerberus but by agreeing on giving her the ring they will create a powerfull and dangerous enemy for the next Story\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4856-alfanumerico","name":"alfanumerico","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}